"desc": "Does the ghost of Mr. Bayless still roam the halls?\n\nJust in time for Halloween, join the Denton County Office of History & Culture for a night of mystery and mayhem at PARK AFTER DARK on Saturday, October 10 at the Denton County Historical Park, 317 W Mulberry Street.\n\nTimed tours are scheduled every 15 minutes from 6 PM to 8 PM, and each tour is limited to 20 people. You must reserve a spot through Eventbrite.com! *Tickets available beginning September 28 at 10 AM!*\n\nOn the night of Saturday November 22, 1919, an argument took place outside the Bayless residence, an argument that ended in death...\n\nTravel through the Bayless-Selby House, located at 317 W Mulberry Street, to hear the accounts of key witnesses and town gossips on what transpired between Samuel Bayless and Joseph Spears that night in 1919. Visitors will also hear from our own volunteers who have experienced more than a few unusual instances inside the house...\n\nFREE event but cash donations are always accepted. Recommended for ages 8 and up. Get a Park After Dark T-shirt with a $20 donation, and stickers available with a $3 donation.\n\nDon't miss this chance to experience the PARK AFTER DARK!",
