"desc": "A Denton tradition celebrating trucks, community and giving!\n\nSince 2016, the Peterbilt Pride & Class Parade has brought truck enthusiasts from across the United States and Canada to Denton for an unforgettable celebration of custom Peterbilt trucks and community spirit. More than 50 impressive trucks make their way through the streets of Denton, culminating in a spectacular parade route through the historic Denton Square.\n\nHeld annually on the third Friday of October, this family-friendly event is a must-see for truck enthusiasts and families alike. Bring your lawn chairs, gather your family and friends, and enjoy a fun-filled evening on the Square as these one-of-a-kind trucks roll through downtown Denton.\n\nBut the Pride & Class Parade is about more than trucks - it's about giving back. Donations from the event support Peterbilt's United Way employee giving campaign, helping make a difference for individuals and families throughout Denton County.\n\nPeterbilt's partnership with United Way of Denton County spans decades. Peterbilt has supported United Way since the 1980s and, since 2002, the partnership has helped raise over $10 million to support the Denton County community. Each fall, Peterbilt employees come together for a week of fundraising, friendly interdepartmental competition and special events - all leading up to the annual Pride & Class Parade.\n\nCome for the trucks. Stay for the fun. Give for the community.\n\nThe Peterbilt Pride & Class Parade is a celebration of pride, class, and the power of people coming together to make a difference.",
