"desc": "The Plum Boys are an Electronic Rock Pop band, formed in 2020 and based in Fort Worth, Texas. Three of the members met while attending school at the Fort Worth Academy of Fine Arts and singing for the world renowned Texas Boys Choir. In their sophomore year of high school and during the pandemic, the boys decided to form a band to write and produce an album. In the final months of their senior year of high school in 2022, they completed their 1st debut album ‘SHE’ and landed a distribution deal through Smith Music out of Fort Worth, Texas.\n\nNot long after the Boys began performing live they were asked to open for the 80’s new wave group ‘A Flock of Seagulls’ at TannaHills Tavern and Music Hall. They recently opened for Kid Bloom at the House of Blues in Dallas and Houston.\n\nIn 2024 The Plum Boys released their 4 song EP ‘Velvet’. Promotion included a summer tour in Fort Worth Texas, Oklahoma, Arkansas and Missouri. Their new EP ‘ALIVE’ is set to release in February 2026, following its 3 singles. This new era of the band ushers in a new sonic landscape and mature tone for the band.\n\nThe Plum Boys are also one of the highest streaming artist on the city of Fort Worth’s Library streaming platform, Amplify817, and have remained on the 91.7 KXT local radio show rotation. They continue to perform locally and regionally while working on building their fan base.",
